.SH NAME
.PP
waybar \- mango keymode module
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBkeymode\fR module displays the current keyboard mode (e.\&g.\& "resize", "default") in the Mango compositor.\& It is hidden when no mode is active.\&
.PP
.SH CONFIGURATION
.PP
Addressed by \fBmango/keymode\fR
.PP
\fBformat\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
default: {} 
.br
The format, how the mode should be displayed.\& \fB{mode}\fR is replaced by the current mode name.\&
.PP
\fBformat\-<mode>\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
Provide a custom format for a specific keymode.\& \fB<mode>\fR is the mode name as reported by Mango (e.\&g.\& "resize").\& The value can contain \fB{mode}\fR as a placeholder.\&
.RS 4
If this option is set, it overrides the main \fBformat\fR for that mode.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBmenu\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
Action that pops up a menu.\&
.PP
\fBmenu\-file\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
Location of the menu descriptor file.\&
.PP
\fBmenu\-actions\fR: 
.br
typeof: array 
.br
Actions for the menu buttons.\&
.PP
\fBexpand\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
Enables the module to consume all leftover space.\&
.PP
.SH FORMAT REPLACEMENTS
.PP
\fB{mode}\fR: The name of the current keymode.\&
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
"mango/keymode": {
	"format": "[{mode}]",
	"format\-resize": " Resizing"
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
.SH STYLE
.PP
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
\fB#keymode\fR
.PD
.PP
A CSS class with the current mode name (e.\&g.\& \fB.\&resize\fR) is added to the widget, allowing per‑mode styling:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
